---
// The homepage's argument for the modular positioning: the four stages of a
// build, each one owned in-house. It sits directly after the stats band and
// before the products grid, so a visitor meets the system before the catalogue.
import { buildStack } from '../data/site.js';
---
<section class="stack" id="how-we-build">
  <div class="stack-inner">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>One Contractor, Frame to Handover</h2>
      <p>Modular only delivers on its promise when the chain isn&rsquo;t split across four suppliers who each blame the last. We own every link of ours.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="stack-grid">
      {buildStack.map((s) => (
        <li class="stack-step">
          <span class="stack-num" aria-hidden="true">{s.step}</span>
          <h3>{s.title}</h3>
          <p>{s.desc}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="stack-note">
      The factory is ours, and so is the designer who draws what it builds. Nothing about your
      frame waits in another company&rsquo;s queue, which is why we can give you a date and a
      price at design stage and hold both.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
